 10 years it wouldn't matter  and do you think anything's changed no  no nearly 10 months on  there's a really strong sense here that  nothing's really changed when it comes  to the treatment of black people by  police  and a real sense of apprehension about  the outcome  of derek shauvin's trial no white police  officer  has ever been convicted for the death of  a black person in minnesota  this time the eyes of the world are  watching  but hope is fragile that george floyd's  death  may change the course of history  sally lockwood sky news minneapolis
 

